virglrenderer: Venus SPIR-V is scanned before the Mac's shader compilers

What: vkCreateShaderModule and SPIR-V chained into a pipeline stage go
through a structural scan (src/venus/vkr_spirv.c, no driver): the header
(magic, version up to 1.6, an id bound up to 2^20, schema 0), every
instruction inside the code, the ids the scan reads inside the bound, entry
point names that end. A pipeline then needs its stage's entry point by name
and execution model, a compute workgroup size after specialization
(LocalSize, LocalSizeId or the WorkgroupSize built-in, spec constants
resolved) inside the device's limits, and every descriptor set and binding
that the functions its entry point reaches use in its layout. Descriptors no
function uses need not be there (glslang lists them in SPIR-V 1.4+
interfaces too). A refusal ends the app's context. The scan also keeps what
virgl-venus-spirv-validate.patch checks before spirv-val: the types of
Function variables (their elements after specialization), the Input and
Output variables with their Location, BuiltIn, Patch and per-vertex
decorations and each entry point's interface (their locations against the
device's limits), and what the types would cost spirv-val's walks over them
(each instruction the weights of the types it names and reads).
Why: KosmicKrisp's spirv_to_nir ended QEMU on a bad magic (NULL in its own
error path) and on an id bound of 0x3fffffff (SIGBUS in
linear_zalloc_child_array); MoltenVK's SPIRV-Cross on garbage, truncated code
and that bound (SIGSEGV) and with an uncaught exception on a missing entry
point or a stage of another model (SIGABRT); Metal ended MoltenVK on a
workgroup of 65536 threads; KosmicKrisp dereferenced a descriptor set the
layout lacks (kk_nir_lower_descriptors).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (spec VUIDs), draft only.
Tests: Tests/virgl/fuzz-venus-spirv.sh (the scan alone on the CPU, under
AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer); Tests/virgl/
test-venus-commands.c (p-spirv-, p-entry-missing, p-stage-mismatch,
p-shader-layout-, p-unused-set-, p-workgroup- cases).

